## What you may do

1. **Read and audit.** View, study and quote the source, including in security
   reviews, articles and discussions.

2. **Build and run it yourself.** Compile the source and run the resulting
   application on machines you own or administer, for your own use or your
   organisation's internal use, without charge.

3. **Modify it for yourself.** Change the source and build from your changes,
   under the same terms, for the same internal use.

4. **Propose changes.** Submit patches, issues and pull requests. By submitting
   a contribution you grant Edward Martin a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable,
   royalty-free licence to use, modify, relicense and distribute it as part of
   this software.

## What you may not do

1. **Redistribute.** Do not publish, share, host or otherwise distribute the
   source, a modified version of it, or any binary built from it, to anyone
   outside your own organisation. Official builds come from the author.

2. **Sell it.** Do not sell, licence, rent or offer the software or any work
   derived from it, whether on its own, as part of a larger product, or as a
   hosted or managed service.

3. **Publish it to an app store.** Do not submit this software, or anything
   derived from it, to the Mac App Store or any other distribution channel.

4. **Remove this notice.** Keep this licence and the copyright notice intact in
   any copy you are permitted to hold.

## Everything else

Other uses require written permission from the author. Requests go to the
address in `SECURITY.md`.

These terms apply to this source tree and to every release after `v0.6.1`.
Releases up to and including `v0.6.1` were published under the MIT licence.
That grant is irrevocable for the copies it was given with, and it stays valid
for anyone who downloads one of those tags or their release assets later: the
licence travels with the copy, not with the project.

Third-party dependencies keep their own licences. The Poppins typeface bundled
with the site is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; see `site/fonts/OFL.txt`.

